    "changelog": [
      "Merged the critic's four candidate rules into [Priority Rules] as demotions: boundaries that end on a bare object NP after a preceding personal name/title, boundaries that end on an ethnonym/demonym before a locative PP or comma-set appositive, boundaries splitting coordinated verb phrases that share a following PP/comparative, and boundaries that cut inside non-finite participial modifiers are all allowed but ranked lower.",
      "Clarified [When to Segment] to instruct the model to still mark these positions as candidates (do not ban) while delegating them to lower confidence per the Priority Rules."
    ],
    "next_changelog": [
      "Strengthened Core Principles with a compact, surface-form heuristic advising the model to MARK risky positions but to demote them in confidence rather than ban them; motivates why verb-object isolation and demonym+locative/appositive cuts are risky for Chinese.",
      "Added an explicit post-ranking 'safety demotion' step to Decision Procedure that (a) detects surface-decidable patterns that previously caused premature/mistranslated boundaries (object-isolating cuts, demonym/ethnonym cuts before PPs/appositives, and comma-cuts followed by PPs or coordinating conjunctions) and (b) pushes those candidates to lower confidence while keeping them as candidates.",
      "Kept [When to Segment], [Priority Rules] and [Output Rules] text unchanged to avoid repeating earlier rejected edits; the new approach operates as an extra conservative reordering stage rather than banning or rewording the priority list."
    ]
  },
